      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Physical Location"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana is situated in northwestern India, bordered by Punjab and Himachal Pradesh to the north, Rajasthan to the south and west, and Uttar Pradesh to the east.",
        "The state is broadly categorized into four physiographic divisions: Shivalik Hills, Yamuna-Ghaggar Alluvial Plains, Semi-desert Sandy Plains, and Aravalli Outliers.",
        "Yamuna River forms the eastern natural boundary, while seasonal rivers like Ghaggar, Markanda, Saraswati, and Tangri drain the northern region.",
        "Major agricultural lands depend on extensive irrigation projects including the Western Yamuna Canal and Bhakra Canal system.",
        "The climate is predominantly subtropical, continental, and semi-arid with hot summers, cool winters, and monsoon rainfall."
      ],
      "id": "niqtvwl"
    },
